{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Shared by the Rust `text` tests and the TypeScript `format` tests (DESIGN 9.9). Frozen: a wrong vector is a contract change.",
    "All local times are in `zone` (a fixed offset, no DST). `now` of the time cases is Monday 14 Dec 2026 12:33:00 local unless a case says otherwise.",
    "percent: whole, rounded down; 0 < x < 1 is '<1%'. percent_detail: one decimal, cut (not rounded), with a space before the sign.",
    "countdown: >= 48 h 'Nd Nh'; >= 1 h 'Nh MMm' (minutes two digits); >= 1 min 'Nm'; below 'under a minute'; reset time not after now is null (the Elapsed state).",
    "absolute: same local day 'today HH:MM'; next local day 'tomorrow HH:MM'; 2 to 6 local days ahead 'Thu HH:MM'; else 'D Mon HH:MM', with the year after the month when it differs from now's. h12 writes 'h:MM AM/PM'.",
    "age: under 1 min (or in the future) 'just now'; under 1 h 'Nm ago'; same local day 'Nh MMm ago'; previous local day 'yesterday HH:MM'; else the date as in absolute.",
    "money: two decimals, half away from zero, English grouping; usd '$', cny 'CN¥'; `other` is the plain number followed by the word 'balance'.",
    "window_name: '5-hour', '7-day', '30-day'; rolling is 'N-day' when a whole number of days, else 'N-hour'; a named window is its raw label."
  ],
  "zone": {
    "name": "Asia/Jakarta",
